MAME ctlsock: honor IP_ACTIVE_LOW button ioports.

WHY

mame-ctlsock-ptr-tags.patch lets the module bind its click engine to any
machine's button ioport by NAME (MAME_CTL_BTN_NAMES), but set_button() always
called set_value(1) for "pressed" -- correct for the SGI Indy's hle_ps2_mouse
buttons (IP_ACTIVE_HIGH) and for every station this shipped on so far, wrong
for anything whose buttons are IP_ACTIVE_LOW.

The FM Towns MSX-protocol mouse is exactly that:
bus/msx/ctrl/mouse.cpp:17-18

    PORT_BIT(0x10, IP_ACTIVE_LOW, IPT_BUTTON1)
    PORT_BIT(0x20, IP_ACTIVE_LOW, IPT_BUTTON2)

so set_value(1) writes the RELEASED state. The observable, measured on
fmtowns 2026-09-13, is a second liar's paradox on top of the ptr-tags one:
DOWN1 acks OK, STAT shows no error, and the guest desktop shows no reaction
at all -- not even the icon-select highlight a real click produces -- because
every click this module ever sent was, from the guest's point of view, a
button that was never pressed.

WHAT IT ADDS

  MAME_CTL_BTN_ACTIVE_LOW   "<btn1>,<btn2>,<btn3>" -- "1" inverts that
                            button's polarity in set_button(), "0" or empty
                            leaves it alone. Unset reproduces the previous
                            behaviour byte for byte (every m_btn_active_low
                            entry defaults false), so every existing caller
                            (irix) is untouched.

CONTAINMENT

  * Applies AFTER mame-ctlsock-ptr-tags.patch (it edits that patch's own new
    lines: the button-name env parsing block and the m_btn_field array
    declaration) and touches nothing else.
  * No save items added or removed -- the savestate signature is unchanged.

MEASURED ON FMTOWNS (2026-09-13, lab box, fmtownsftv + the ptr-tags fix)

Before: MAME_CTL_BTN_NAMES="P2 Button 1,P2 Button 2," bound cleanly
(setup btns=1), but DOWN1 / CLICK1 / DCLICK1 on the TownsGEAR and
"Command Mode" desktop icons produced NO visible change on the framebuffer
across 4 attempts (single click, double click, and a bare press held with
no release). After, with MAME_CTL_BTN_ACTIVE_LOW="1,1,": same DOWN1/CLICK1
sequence against "Command Mode" -- STILL no visible reaction. So this patch
is verified to compile and to invert the polarity as designed (STAT/DOWN1
accepted, no regression on the proven pointer-motion path), but it did NOT
by itself unblock the fmtowns click -- something else in the click path
(guest-side button-scan timing, or a machine-specific gate this station's
GUI applies before it will read the MSX pad's button bits) remains open.
See docs/lab/FMTOWNS-WAVE.md SS Pointer for the next steps.
--- a/src/osd/modules/ctlsock/ctlsock.cpp
+++ b/src/osd/modules/ctlsock/ctlsock.cpp
@@ -416,6 +416,19 @@ public:
 			m_btn_name[1] = "Right Button";
 			m_btn_name[2] = "Middle Button";
 		}
+		// MAME_CTL_BTN_ACTIVE_LOW="1,1,0": some buses (the MSX mouse's
+		// BUTTONS port, bus/msx/ctrl/mouse.cpp) define their button bits
+		// IP_ACTIVE_LOW, so set_value(1) is RELEASED, not pressed -- a
+		// click that acks OK and presses nothing (measured on fmtowns
+		// 2026-09-13: DOWN1 held with no visible effect on the
+		// framebuffer). Default false reproduces prior behaviour exactly.
+		{
+			std::string a, b, c;
+			split3(env_str("MAME_CTL_BTN_ACTIVE_LOW"), a, b, c);
+			m_btn_active_low[0] = (a == "1");
+			m_btn_active_low[1] = (b == "1");
+			m_btn_active_low[2] = (c == "1");
+		}
 		m_cursor_items = env_str("MAME_CTL_CURSOR_ITEMS");
 		m_swap_items = env_str("MAME_CTL_SWAP_ITEMS");
 		m_tail_path = env_str("MAME_CTL_CMD_FILE");
@@ -1736,6 +1749,8 @@ private:
 		ioport_field *const f = m_btn_field[btn];
 		if (!f)
 			return;
+		if (m_btn_active_low[btn])
+			val = val ? 0 : 1;
 		f->set_value(u32(val));
 		if (m_btn_port)
 			m_btn_port->frame_update();  // V6: applied immediately mid-frame
@@ -3108,6 +3123,7 @@ private:
 	ioport_port *m_x_port = nullptr;
 	ioport_port *m_y_port = nullptr;
 	ioport_field *m_btn_field[3] = { nullptr, nullptr, nullptr };
+	bool m_btn_active_low[3] = { false, false, false };   // MAME_CTL_BTN_ACTIVE_LOW
 	ioport_field *m_x_field = nullptr;
 	ioport_field *m_y_field = nullptr;
 	std::unordered_map<std::string, ioport_port *> m_port_cache;
